# A session asks a question while the user is away. The phone gets the question with
# its field and choices, numbered. A reply is refused at once with where to answer,
# not queued behind a turn: the turn cannot end until the question is answered, so
# "when this turn ends" would never come. Once the question is answered at the PC, an
# ordinary reply goes into the composer as before. (Answering from the phone itself is
# a separate piece of work.)

size 110x30
arg --mux
fake_telegram private
session existing-app Existing app session

wait_for Existing app session
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot is idling

type e2e:ask 1500 Which colour should the header be? | Red | Green | Blue
press enter
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session

telegram_wait Question waiting for your response
telegram_wait Question: Which colour should the header be?
telegram_wait <b>Your answer</b>
telegram_wait 1. Red
telegram_wait 3. Blue
telegram_dump 01-question
dump 01-list-with-question

telegram_say Blue please
wait 4000
telegram_wait Not delivered: Existing app session is waiting on a question
telegram_expect_not Queued
telegram_expect_not reaction on
telegram_dump 02-refused

# Answered at the PC: the turn ends and the session takes ordinary replies again.
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot asked
type e2e:answered Blue
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot finished a turn.
press ctrl+b d
wait_for Existing app session
telegram_say Thanks, now write the footer
wait 4000
press enter
wait_for Fake Copilot received: Thanks, now write the footer
telegram_wait reaction on
telegram_dump 03-after-answer
dump 03-reply-delivered
